    "title": "Working from Home: Two Views",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "More and more people now work from home. Some love it, and others do not. Here are the opinions of two workers, Jack and Priya."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Jack says: 'I work from home three days a week, and I love it. I save two hours every day because I don't travel to the office. I also save money on petrol and lunch. At home, it is quiet, so I can concentrate better. I can also take a short break to walk my dog. My boss trusts me, and I finish all my work.'"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Priya says: 'I tried working from home last year, but I did not enjoy it. I live in a small flat with two other people, so it is noisy. I miss my colleagues, too. In the office, we have coffee together and talk about our weekends. At home, I felt lonely. Now I work in the office four days a week and at home on Fridays. That is perfect for me.'"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Experts say that both ways of working have good and bad points. Working from home can save time and money, but some people feel alone. A mixed system, with some days at home and some days at the office, is becoming popular in many companies. Whatever you choose, it is important to have a quiet place to work and to talk to your colleagues regularly."
      }
    ]
  },
